import Mathlib
import HolonicsResearch.Landmarks.Sieve

/-!
# The first-arrival sieve tower of a multiplicative recurrence with a size

[definition] Setting. A commutative monoid `M` is a multiplicative recurrence: its elements are reached from `1` by
products. A **size** is a monoid map `N : M →* ℕ` with `1 < N x` for every `x ≠ 1` (`IsSize`); then `N x = 1` only at
`x = 1` (`IsSize.eq_one_iff`), `1` is the only unit (`IsSize.isUnit_iff`) and a proper factor is smaller
(`IsSize.lt_of_mul`). A **first arrival** (an atom) is `x ≠ 1` that is no product of two elements other than `1`
(`Atom`); with a size these are Mathlib's irreducibles (`atom_iff_irreducible`). The survivors of a set `P` of
admitted atoms are the elements none of them divides (`survivors`), and the sieve's level at grain `t` admits the
atoms of size at most `t` (`level`). No cancellation and no unique factorization is assumed.

The reading of #410's "beyond Eratosthenes" is `agent-inferred`: the sieve tower is read as a law of every
multiplicative recurrence with a size, not of `ℕ`'s primes alone, and it is proved without unique factorization;
Hilbert's monoid is the instance where factorization into first arrivals is plural.

Sources: #410's box "Möbius and quadratic landmarks: … the first-arrival sieve tower beyond Eratosthenes" (its other
clauses are `Compression/Landmark/AffineLandmark`, whose "Limits" paragraph names this one);
`Holonics/Compression/Landmark`'s `[open]` paragraph ("the first-arrival sieve tower as a general law"); the record
`2026-09-24_THE_NULL_CONE_IS_THE_CONSTITUTIONS_LOCK_AND_CLOSURE_IS_A_RECEIVER_READING` §5 ("the sieve is an epoch
tower whose survivors are the first arrivals of the multiplicative recurrence"); `docs/WINDING_CARRY_AND_PLACEMENT.md`
§7 (a growing sieve removes the multiples of admitted primes, and coverage through `√n` decides primality); the
house's first-arrival populations (`Computation/HolonicRecurrentEcology.FirstArrival`); the `ℕ` owner
`Landmarks/Sieve`; atlas rows `landmark.sieve-epoch-tower`, `landmark.eratosthenes`, `landmark.sieve-first-arrival`,
`landmark.sieve-grain-counterexample`, `winding.crt-diagonal`, `navigator.first-arrival`.

[proved-standard; formal-checked] What is proved.

1. **Every element is a finite product of first arrivals** (`exists_atom_factors`, by strong induction on the size;
   `1` is the empty product), so every `x ≠ 1` has a first-arrival divisor (`exists_atom_dvd`). A first arrival is
   the element the recurrence reaches first at its own size: `x` is an atom when and only when `x ≠ 1` and `x` lies
   outside the submonoid generated by the elements of smaller size (`atom_iff_not_mem_closure`).
2. **The tower.** The levels grow with the grain (`level_mono`) and the survivors shrink (`survivors_anti`,
   `survivors_level_antitone`). Each step of the grain is one residue condition at the atoms it admits: the survivors
   of level `t + 1` are those of level `t` that no atom of size `t + 1` divides (`survivors_level_succ`). `1`
   survives every level (`one_mem_survivors_level`), every `x ≠ 1` is sieved by the level of its own size at the
   latest (`not_mem_survivors_level`), and the tower's intersection is `{1}` (`iInter_survivors_level`).
   - (a) **An atom survives every level below its size and is sieved at its size**
     (`atom_mem_survivors_level_iff`: an atom `x` survives level `t` when and only when `t < N x`).
   - (b) **First arrival.** Every non-identity survivor of least size, under any admitted set, is an atom
     (`atom_of_least_survivor`); at level `t` it is an atom of size above `t` (`least_survivor_level`). A
     non-identity survivor of level `t` has an atom divisor of size in `(t, N x]` (`survivor_atom_dvd`), and the
     least size of a non-identity survivor of level `t` is the least size of an atom above `t`
     (`isLeast_survivor_size_iff`).
   - (c) **Coverage through the square root.** If `x ≠ 1` and no atom `p` with `N p * N p ≤ N x` divides `x`, then
     `x` is an atom (`atom_of_no_small_atom_dvd`, from 1). In the tower: a non-identity survivor of level `t` with
     `N x < (t + 1)²` is an atom (`atom_of_survivor_lt_sq`, `mem_survivors_level_iff_of_lt_sq`), and `x ≠ 1` is an
     atom when and only when it survives the level `⌊√(N x)⌋` (`atom_iff_mem_survivors_sqrt`).
3. **The instance `ℕ+`, size the number itself.** Its first arrivals are the primes (`pnat_isSize`,
   `pnat_atom_iff_prime`, `pnat_mem_level`), and 2(c) is Eratosthenes' coverage (`eratosthenes`,
   `eratosthenes_level`). The tower's survivors are `Landmarks/Sieve`'s (`pnat_survivors_iff_sieve`).
4. **Hilbert's monoid** `{n : ℕ | n % 4 = 1}` under multiplication, size the number itself (`hilbert`,
   `hilbert_isSize`, `hilbert_atom_iff`): items 1 and 2 hold there as they stand. `9`, `21` and `49` are atoms
   (`hilbert_atoms`) and `9 · 49 = 21 · 21 = 441` (`hilbert_mul`), so factorization into first arrivals is plural
   (`hilbert_factorization_plural`), and a first arrival need not be prime: `21 ∣ 9 · 49` with `21 ∤ 9` and
   `21 ∤ 49` (`hilbert_atom_not_prime`).
5. **Monic polynomials over a finite field** `K` with `q = |K|`, size `q ^ deg f` (`monics`, `polySize`,
   `polySize_isSize`): the first arrivals are the monic irreducibles (`monic_atom_iff_irreducible`), every monic is a
   product of monic irreducibles (`monic_factors`), and coverage reads: a monic `f ≠ 1` with no monic irreducible
   factor `g` of `2 deg g ≤ deg f` is irreducible (`irreducible_of_no_small_factor`).

What is not claimed. Nothing on prime gaps, densities, Kac's mean-gap form or Cramér's model: the record's
`[interpretation]` of the mean gap stays one. Uniqueness of factorization is not assumed and, by item 4, does not
follow. The general monoid has no canonical least atom divisor, so the recurrence `m ↦ m / minFac m` of
`Landmarks/Sieve` (whose first arrivals at the unit receiver are counted by `Ω`) is not generalized; the first-arrival
reading here is the closure law of item 1 and the least survivor of item 2(b). Sizes are natural numbers; a real-valued
norm is not treated, and no finiteness of the set of atoms of a given size is used or proved.

The computational object is the helical pair interaction: here a multiplicative recurrence whose first arrivals are
its atoms, each sieve level a residue condition at an admitted atom (`p ∤ x`: `x` stands off the multiples of `p`,
a condition admitted at the level `N p`). Of the winding guide's six general objects this touches the tower thread
(the levels are a nested tower of sections, and the grain `⌊√(N x)⌋` is where coverage closes) and faces and
placement (a level's survivors are a face read at a declared grain); the helix, the pair, cell holonomy and the tube
stay attached.

Consumers: #410's box "Möbius and quadratic landmarks: … the first-arrival sieve tower beyond Eratosthenes";
`Holonics/Compression/Landmark`'s `[open]` clause on the sieve tower as a general law; `Landmarks/Sieve`, whose
survivors are the `ℕ+` instance's (`pnat_survivors_iff_sieve`).

No `sorry`, no `axiom`, no `native_decide`.
-/

namespace Holonics.Compression.Landmark.SieveTower

/-! ## 1. A size, and the first arrivals -/

section General

variable {M : Type*} [CommMonoid M]

/-- [definition] **A first arrival (an atom)**: an element other than `1` that is no product of two elements other
than `1`. -/
def Atom (x : M) : Prop := x ≠ 1 ∧ ∀ y z, x = y * z → y = 1 ∨ z = 1

/-- [definition] **A size**: a monoid map to `ℕ` that exceeds `1` off the identity. -/
def IsSize (N : M →* ℕ) : Prop := ∀ x, x ≠ 1 → 1 < N x

variable {N : M →* ℕ}

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A size is positive. -/
theorem IsSize.pos (hN : IsSize N) (x : M) : 0 < N x := by
  by_cases hx : x = 1
  · simp [hx]
  · exact Nat.zero_lt_one.trans (hN x hx)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The size is `1` only at the identity. -/
theorem IsSize.eq_one_iff (hN : IsSize N) {x : M} : N x = 1 ↔ x = 1 := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    by_contra hx
    exact (hN x hx).ne' h
  · rintro rfl
    exact map_one N

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A divisor is no larger than what it divides. -/
theorem IsSize.le_of_dvd (hN : IsSize N) {y x : M} (h : y ∣ x) : N y ≤ N x := by
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := h
  rw [map_mul]
  exact Nat.le_mul_of_pos_right _ (hN.pos c)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A proper factor is smaller. -/
theorem IsSize.lt_of_mul (hN : IsSize N) (y : M) {z : M} (hz : z ≠ 1) : N y < N (y * z) := by
  rw [map_mul]
  exact lt_mul_of_one_lt_right (hN.pos y) (hN z hz)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The identity is the only unit. -/
theorem IsSize.isUnit_iff (hN : IsSize N) {x : M} : IsUnit x ↔ x = 1 := by
  constructor
  · intro h
    obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := isUnit_iff_exists_inv.mp h
    have h1 : N x * N y = 1 := by rw [← map_mul, hy, map_one]
    exact hN.eq_one_iff.mp (Nat.eq_one_of_mul_eq_one_right h1)
  · rintro rfl
    exact isUnit_one

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] With a size, the first arrivals are the irreducibles. -/
theorem atom_iff_irreducible (hN : IsSize N) {x : M} : Atom x ↔ Irreducible x := by
  rw [irreducible_iff]
  simp only [hN.isUnit_iff, Atom]

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] An element other than `1` that is no atom splits into two factors other than
`1`. -/
theorem exists_mul_of_not_atom {x : M} (h1 : x ≠ 1) (ha : ¬ Atom x) :
    ∃ y z, x = y * z ∧ y ≠ 1 ∧ z ≠ 1 := by
  unfold Atom at ha
  push Not at ha
  exact ha h1

/-! ## 2. Every element is a finite product of first arrivals -/

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **Every element is a finite product of atoms**, `1` the empty product. -/
theorem exists_atom_factors (hN : IsSize N) (x : M) :
    ∃ s : Multiset M, (∀ a ∈ s, Atom a) ∧ s.prod = x := by
  suffices H : ∀ n, ∀ x : M, N x = n → ∃ s : Multiset M, (∀ a ∈ s, Atom a) ∧ s.prod = x from H _ x rfl
  intro n
  induction n using Nat.strong_induction_on with
  | _ n ih =>
    intro x hx
    by_cases h1 : x = 1
    · exact ⟨0, by simp, by simp [h1]⟩
    by_cases ha : Atom x
    · exact ⟨{x}, by simpa using ha, by simp⟩
    obtain ⟨y, z, rfl, hy, hz⟩ := exists_mul_of_not_atom h1 ha
    obtain ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩ := ih (N y) (hx ▸ hN.lt_of_mul y hz) y rfl
    obtain ⟨u, hu, rfl⟩ := ih (N z) (hx ▸ mul_comm z s.prod ▸ hN.lt_of_mul z hy) z rfl
    refine ⟨s + u, fun a ha => ?_, Multiset.prod_add s u⟩
    rcases Multiset.mem_add.mp ha with h | h
    · exact hs a h
    · exact hu a h

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Every element other than `1` has an atom divisor. -/
theorem exists_atom_dvd (hN : IsSize N) {x : M} (hx : x ≠ 1) : ∃ p, Atom p ∧ p ∣ x := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩ := exists_atom_factors hN x
  have hs0 : s ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    exact hx Multiset.prod_zero
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := Multiset.exists_mem_of_ne_zero hs0
  exact ⟨a, hs a ha, Multiset.dvd_prod ha⟩

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A product of a list that is an atom is one of the list's entries. -/
theorem prod_mem_of_atom {l : List M} (h : Atom l.prod) : l.prod ∈ l := by
  induction l with
  | nil => exact absurd List.prod_nil h.1
  | cons a t ih =>
    rw [List.prod_cons] at h ⊢
    rcases h.2 a t.prod rfl with ha | ht
    · subst ha
      rw [one_mul] at h ⊢
      exact List.mem_cons_of_mem 1 (ih h)
    · rw [ht, mul_one]
      exact List.mem_cons_self

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **An atom is a first arrival**: `x` is an atom when and only when `x ≠ 1` and
the products of elements of smaller size do not reach it. -/
theorem atom_iff_not_mem_closure (hN : IsSize N) {x : M} :
    Atom x ↔ x ≠ 1 ∧ x ∉ Submonoid.closure {y | N y < N x} := by
  constructor
  · intro ha
    refine ⟨ha.1, fun hx => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨l, hl, hprod⟩ := Submonoid.exists_list_of_mem_closure hx
    have hmem := prod_mem_of_atom (hprod ▸ ha)
    have hlt : N l.prod < N x := hl _ hmem
    rw [hprod] at hlt
    exact lt_irrefl _ hlt
  · rintro ⟨h1, hx⟩
    refine ⟨h1, fun y z hyz => ?_⟩
    by_contra hne
    push Not at hne
    apply hx
    have hy : N y < N x := hyz ▸ hN.lt_of_mul y hne.2
    have hz : N z < N x := hyz ▸ mul_comm z y ▸ hN.lt_of_mul z hne.1
    have hm : y * z ∈ Submonoid.closure {w | N w < N x} :=
      Submonoid.mul_mem _ (Submonoid.subset_closure hy) (Submonoid.subset_closure hz)
    rwa [← hyz] at hm

/-! ## 3. The sieve tower -/

/-- [definition] **The survivors** of a set `P` of admitted atoms: the elements none of them divides. -/
def survivors (P : Set M) : Set M := {x | ∀ p ∈ P, ¬ p ∣ x}

/-- [definition] **The sieve's level at grain `t`**: the atoms of size at most `t`. -/
def level (N : M →* ℕ) (t : ℕ) : Set M := {p | Atom p ∧ N p ≤ t}

/-- [definition] Membership in the survivors, unfolded. -/
theorem mem_survivors {P : Set M} {x : M} : x ∈ survivors P ↔ ∀ p ∈ P, ¬ p ∣ x := Iff.rfl

/-- [definition] Membership in a level, unfolded. -/
theorem mem_level {t : ℕ} {p : M} : p ∈ level N t ↔ Atom p ∧ N p ≤ t := Iff.rfl

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Admitting more atoms leaves fewer survivors. -/
theorem survivors_anti {P Q : Set M} (h : P ⊆ Q) : survivors Q ⊆ survivors P :=
  fun _ hx p hp => hx p (h hp)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The levels grow with the grain. -/
theorem level_mono {t t' : ℕ} (h : t ≤ t') : level N t ⊆ level N t' :=
  fun _ hp => ⟨hp.1, hp.2.trans h⟩

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The tower**: the survivors shrink as the grain rises. -/
theorem survivors_level_antitone : Antitone fun t => survivors (level N t) :=
  fun _ _ h => survivors_anti (level_mono h)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **One step of the grain is one residue condition**: the survivors of level
`t + 1` are those of level `t` that no atom of size `t + 1` divides. -/
theorem survivors_level_succ (t : ℕ) :
    survivors (level N (t + 1)) = survivors (level N t) ∩ {x | ∀ p, Atom p → N p = t + 1 → ¬ p ∣ x} := by
  ext x
  simp only [survivors, level, Set.mem_inter_iff]
  constructor
  · intro h
    exact ⟨fun p hp => h p ⟨hp.1, hp.2.trans (Nat.le_succ t)⟩, fun p hp hpt => h p ⟨hp, hpt.le⟩⟩
  · rintro ⟨h, h'⟩ p ⟨hp, hpt⟩
    rcases Nat.lt_or_eq_of_le hpt with hlt | heq
    · exact h p ⟨hp, Nat.lt_succ_iff.mp hlt⟩
    · exact h' p hp heq

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] `1` survives every level. -/
theorem one_mem_survivors_level (hN : IsSize N) (t : ℕ) : (1 : M) ∈ survivors (level N t) := by
  intro p hp hdvd
  have h1 : N p ≤ 1 := map_one N ▸ hN.le_of_dvd hdvd
  exact hp.1.1 (hN.eq_one_iff.mp (le_antisymm h1 (hN.pos p)))

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Every `x ≠ 1` is sieved by the level of its own size at the latest. -/
theorem not_mem_survivors_level (hN : IsSize N) {x : M} (hx : x ≠ 1) {t : ℕ} (ht : N x ≤ t) :
    x ∉ survivors (level N t) := by
  intro hs
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hpx⟩ := exists_atom_dvd hN hx
  exact hs p ⟨hp, (hN.le_of_dvd hpx).trans ht⟩ hpx

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The tower's intersection is `{1}`. -/
theorem iInter_survivors_level (hN : IsSize N) : ⋂ t, survivors (level N t) = {(1 : M)} := by
  ext x
  simp only [Set.mem_iInter, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
  constructor
  · intro h
    by_contra hx
    exact not_mem_survivors_level hN hx le_rfl (h (N x))
  · rintro rfl t
    exact one_mem_survivors_level hN t

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **(a) An atom survives level `t` when and only when `t < N x`**: below its size no
admitted atom divides it, and at its size it divides itself. -/
theorem atom_mem_survivors_level_iff {x : M} (ha : Atom x) {t : ℕ} :
    x ∈ survivors (level N t) ↔ t < N x := by
  constructor
  · intro hs
    by_contra hle
    exact hs x ⟨ha, not_lt.mp hle⟩ dvd_rfl
  · rintro ht p ⟨hp, hpt⟩ ⟨c, hc⟩
    rcases ha.2 p c hc with h | h
    · exact hp.1 h
    · rw [h, mul_one] at hc
      rw [hc] at ht
      exact absurd hpt (not_le.mpr ht)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **(b) A non-identity survivor of least size is an atom**, under any admitted
set. -/
theorem atom_of_least_survivor (hN : IsSize N) {P : Set M} {x : M} (hx : x ∈ survivors P) (hx1 : x ≠ 1)
    (hmin : ∀ y ∈ survivors P, y ≠ 1 → N x ≤ N y) : Atom x := by
  refine ⟨hx1, fun y z hyz => ?_⟩
  by_contra hne
  push Not at hne
  have hy : y ∈ survivors P := fun p hp hpy => hx p hp (hyz ▸ dvd_mul_of_dvd_left hpy z)
  have hlt : N y < N x := hyz ▸ hN.lt_of_mul y hne.2
  exact absurd (hmin y hy hne.1) (not_le.mpr hlt)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **(b) At level `t` the least non-identity survivor is an atom of size above
`t`**: the next first arrival. -/
theorem least_survivor_level (hN : IsSize N) {t : ℕ} {x : M} (hx : x ∈ survivors (level N t)) (hx1 : x ≠ 1)
    (hmin : ∀ y ∈ survivors (level N t), y ≠ 1 → N x ≤ N y) : Atom x ∧ t < N x := by
  have ha := atom_of_least_survivor hN hx hx1 hmin
  exact ⟨ha, (atom_mem_survivors_level_iff ha).mp hx⟩

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A non-identity survivor of level `t` has an atom divisor of size in
`(t, N x]`. -/
theorem survivor_atom_dvd (hN : IsSize N) {t : ℕ} {x : M} (hx : x ∈ survivors (level N t)) (hx1 : x ≠ 1) :
    ∃ p, Atom p ∧ p ∣ x ∧ t < N p ∧ N p ≤ N x := by
  obtain ⟨p, hp, hpx⟩ := exists_atom_dvd hN hx1
  refine ⟨p, hp, hpx, ?_, hN.le_of_dvd hpx⟩
  by_contra hle
  exact hx p ⟨hp, not_lt.mp hle⟩ hpx

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **(b) First arrival**: the least size of a non-identity survivor of level `t`
is the least size of an atom above `t`. -/
theorem isLeast_survivor_size_iff (hN : IsSize N) (t n : ℕ) :
    IsLeast {m | ∃ x ∈ survivors (level N t), x ≠ 1 ∧ N x = m} n ↔
      IsLeast {m | ∃ p, Atom p ∧ t < N p ∧ N p = m} n := by
  have hsub : ∀ m, m ∈ {m | ∃ p, Atom p ∧ t < N p ∧ N p = m} →
      m ∈ {m | ∃ x ∈ survivors (level N t), x ≠ 1 ∧ N x = m} := by
    rintro m ⟨p, hp, hpt, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨p, (atom_mem_survivors_level_iff hp).mpr hpt, hp.1, rfl⟩
  have hbelow : ∀ m, m ∈ {m | ∃ x ∈ survivors (level N t), x ≠ 1 ∧ N x = m} →
      ∃ b ∈ {m | ∃ p, Atom p ∧ t < N p ∧ N p = m}, b ≤ m := by
    rintro m ⟨x, hx, hx1, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨p, hp, -, hpt, hle⟩ := survivor_atom_dvd hN hx hx1
    exact ⟨N p, ⟨p, hp, hpt, rfl⟩, hle⟩
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨hn, hlow⟩
    obtain ⟨b, hb, hbn⟩ := hbelow n hn
    have hnb : n ≤ b := hlow (hsub b hb)
    refine ⟨le_antisymm hbn hnb ▸ hb, fun m hm => hlow (hsub m hm)⟩
  · rintro ⟨hn, hlow⟩
    refine ⟨hsub n hn, fun m hm => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨b, hb, hbm⟩ := hbelow m hm
    exact (hlow hb).trans hbm

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **(c) Coverage through the square root**: an `x ≠ 1` that no atom `p` with
`N p * N p ≤ N x` divides is an atom. -/
theorem atom_of_no_small_atom_dvd (hN : IsSize N) {x : M} (hx : x ≠ 1)
    (h : ∀ p, Atom p → N p * N p ≤ N x → ¬ p ∣ x) : Atom x := by
  have key : ∀ y z, x = y * z → y ≠ 1 → N y ≤ N z → False := by
    intro y z hyz hy hle
    obtain ⟨p, hp, hpy⟩ := exists_atom_dvd hN hy
    have hpN : N p ≤ N y := hN.le_of_dvd hpy
    have hsq : N p * N p ≤ N x := by
      rw [hyz, map_mul]
      exact Nat.mul_le_mul hpN (hpN.trans hle)
    exact h p hp hsq (hpy.trans ⟨z, hyz⟩)
  refine ⟨hx, fun y z hyz => ?_⟩
  by_contra hne
  push Not at hne
  rcases le_total (N y) (N z) with hle | hle
  · exact key y z hyz hne.1 hle
  · exact key z y (hyz.trans (mul_comm y z)) hne.2 hle

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **(c) in the tower**: a non-identity survivor of level `t` with
`N x < (t + 1)²` is an atom. -/
theorem atom_of_survivor_lt_sq (hN : IsSize N) {t : ℕ} {x : M} (hx : x ∈ survivors (level N t)) (hx1 : x ≠ 1)
    (hlt : N x < (t + 1) * (t + 1)) : Atom x := by
  refine atom_of_no_small_atom_dvd hN hx1 fun p hp hsq => hx p ⟨hp, ?_⟩
  by_contra hle
  have h' : (t + 1) * (t + 1) ≤ N p * N p := Nat.mul_self_le_mul_self (not_le.mp hle)
  omega

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Below `(t + 1)²` the survivors of level `t` other than `1` are the atoms of
size above `t`. -/
theorem mem_survivors_level_iff_of_lt_sq (hN : IsSize N) {t : ℕ} {x : M} (hx1 : x ≠ 1)
    (hlt : N x < (t + 1) * (t + 1)) : x ∈ survivors (level N t) ↔ Atom x ∧ t < N x := by
  constructor
  · intro hx
    have ha := atom_of_survivor_lt_sq hN hx hx1 hlt
    exact ⟨ha, (atom_mem_survivors_level_iff ha).mp hx⟩
  · rintro ⟨ha, ht⟩
    exact (atom_mem_survivors_level_iff ha).mpr ht

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **(c) at the grain `⌊√(N x)⌋`**: `x ≠ 1` is an atom when and only when it
survives that level. -/
theorem atom_iff_mem_survivors_sqrt (hN : IsSize N) {x : M} (hx1 : x ≠ 1) :
    Atom x ↔ x ∈ survivors (level N (Nat.sqrt (N x))) := by
  constructor
  · intro ha
    exact (atom_mem_survivors_level_iff ha).mpr (Nat.sqrt_lt_self (hN x hx1))
  · intro hx
    exact atom_of_no_small_atom_dvd hN hx1 fun p hp hsq => hx p ⟨hp, Nat.le_sqrt.mpr hsq⟩

end General

/-! ## 4. The instance `ℕ+`: the first arrivals are the primes -/

section PNat

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The number itself is a size on `ℕ+`. -/
theorem pnat_isSize : IsSize PNat.coeMonoidHom := by
  intro x hx
  have h1 : (x : ℕ) ≠ 1 := fun h => hx (PNat.coe_eq_one_iff.mp h)
  have h0 := x.pos
  change 1 < (x : ℕ)
  omega

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The first arrivals of `ℕ+` are the primes.** -/
theorem pnat_atom_iff_prime (n : ℕ+) : Atom n ↔ (n : ℕ).Prime := by
  rw [Nat.prime_def]
  constructor
  · intro ha
    refine ⟨pnat_isSize n ha.1, fun m hm => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨k, hk⟩ := hm
    have hm0 : 0 < m := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero (by rintro rfl; simp at hk)
    have hk0 : 0 < k := Nat.pos_of_ne_zero (by rintro rfl; simp at hk)
    rcases ha.2 ⟨m, hm0⟩ ⟨k, hk0⟩ (PNat.eq hk) with h | h
    · exact Or.inl (congrArg PNat.val h)
    · have hk1 : k = 1 := congrArg PNat.val h
      subst hk1
      exact Or.inr (by rw [hk, mul_one])
  · rintro ⟨h2, hdiv⟩
    refine ⟨fun h => by rw [h] at h2; simp at h2, fun y z hyz => ?_⟩
    have hyz' : (n : ℕ) = y * z := congrArg PNat.val hyz
    rcases hdiv y ⟨z, hyz'⟩ with h | h
    · exact Or.inl (PNat.coe_eq_one_iff.mp h)
    · right
      apply PNat.coe_eq_one_iff.mp
      have hn0 := n.pos
      rw [h] at hyz'
      exact (Nat.mul_eq_left hn0.ne').mp hyz'.symm

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The level at grain `t` admits the primes up to `t`. -/
theorem pnat_mem_level (t : ℕ) (p : ℕ+) : p ∈ level PNat.coeMonoidHom t ↔ (p : ℕ).Prime ∧ (p : ℕ) ≤ t := by
  rw [mem_level, pnat_atom_iff_prime]
  rfl

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **Eratosthenes' coverage**, read from the general law: `n ≥ 2` that no prime
`p` with `p * p ≤ n` divides is prime. -/
theorem eratosthenes (n : ℕ) (hn : 2 ≤ n) (h : ∀ p, p.Prime → p * p ≤ n → ¬ p ∣ n) : n.Prime := by
  have hpos : 0 < n := by omega
  have hx1 : (⟨n, hpos⟩ : ℕ+) ≠ 1 := by
    intro h1
    have : n = 1 := congrArg PNat.val h1
    omega
  refine (pnat_atom_iff_prime ⟨n, hpos⟩).mp (atom_of_no_small_atom_dvd pnat_isSize hx1 fun p hp hsq hdvd => ?_)
  exact h p ((pnat_atom_iff_prime p).mp hp) hsq (PNat.dvd_iff.mp hdvd)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Eratosthenes at the grain `⌊√n⌋`: `n ≥ 2` that survives the primes up to
`⌊√n⌋` is prime, and a prime survives them. -/
theorem eratosthenes_level (n : ℕ+) (hn : n ≠ 1) :
    (n : ℕ).Prime ↔ ∀ p : ℕ, p.Prime → p ≤ Nat.sqrt n → ¬ p ∣ n := by
  rw [← pnat_atom_iff_prime, atom_iff_mem_survivors_sqrt pnat_isSize hn]
  constructor
  · intro hs p hp hpt hdvd
    have hp0 : 0 < p := hp.pos
    exact hs ⟨p, hp0⟩ ((pnat_mem_level _ _).mpr ⟨hp, hpt⟩) (PNat.dvd_iff.mpr hdvd)
  · intro h p hp hdvd
    obtain ⟨hpp, hpt⟩ := (pnat_mem_level _ _).mp hp
    exact h p hpp hpt (PNat.dvd_iff.mp hdvd)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The tower's survivors are `Landmarks/Sieve`'s**: below `B`, a number other
than `1` survives level `t` when and only when it lies in `Sieve.survivors t B`. -/
theorem pnat_survivors_iff_sieve (t B : ℕ) (n : ℕ+) :
    (n : ℕ) ∈ Holonics.Landmarks.Sieve.survivors t B ↔
      n ≠ 1 ∧ (n : ℕ) < B ∧ n ∈ survivors (level PNat.coeMonoidHom t) := by
  rw [Holonics.Landmarks.Sieve.mem_survivors]
  have hn := n.pos
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨h1, hB, hall⟩
    refine ⟨fun h => by rw [h] at h1; simp at h1, hB, fun p hp hdvd => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨hpp, hpt⟩ := (pnat_mem_level _ _).mp hp
    exact hall p hpp hpt (PNat.dvd_iff.mp hdvd)
  · rintro ⟨h1, hB, hs⟩
    have h1' : (n : ℕ) ≠ 1 := fun h => h1 (PNat.coe_eq_one_iff.mp h)
    refine ⟨by omega, hB, fun p hp hpt hdvd => ?_⟩
    exact hs ⟨p, hp.pos⟩ ((pnat_mem_level _ _).mpr ⟨hp, hpt⟩) (PNat.dvd_iff.mpr hdvd)

end PNat

/-! ## 5. Hilbert's monoid: the tower holds and factorization is plural -/

section Hilbert

/-- [definition] **Hilbert's monoid**: the numbers `≡ 1 (mod 4)` under multiplication. -/
def hilbert : Submonoid ℕ where
  carrier := {n | n % 4 = 1}
  one_mem' := rfl
  mul_mem' := by
    intro a b ha hb
    change a % 4 = 1 at ha
    change b % 4 = 1 at hb
    change a * b % 4 = 1
    rw [Nat.mul_mod, ha, hb]

/-- [definition] Membership in Hilbert's monoid, unfolded. -/
theorem mem_hilbert {n : ℕ} : n ∈ hilbert ↔ n % 4 = 1 := Iff.rfl

/-- [definition] The element `n` of Hilbert's monoid, its residue checked by `decide`. -/
def hil (n : ℕ) (h : n % 4 = 1 := by decide) : hilbert := ⟨n, h⟩

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] The number itself is a size on Hilbert's monoid. -/
theorem hilbert_isSize : IsSize hilbert.subtype := by
  intro x hx
  have h4 : (x : ℕ) % 4 = 1 := x.2
  have h1 : (x : ℕ) ≠ 1 := fun h => hx (OneMemClass.coe_eq_one.mp h)
  change 1 < (x : ℕ)
  omega

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The first arrivals of Hilbert's monoid**: `x ≠ 1` whose only divisors
`≡ 1 (mod 4)` are `1` and `x`. -/
theorem hilbert_atom_iff (x : hilbert) :
    Atom x ↔ (x : ℕ) ≠ 1 ∧ ∀ d, d ∣ (x : ℕ) → d % 4 = 1 → d = 1 ∨ d = x := by
  have hx4 : (x : ℕ) % 4 = 1 := x.2
  constructor
  · intro ha
    refine ⟨fun h => ha.1 (OneMemClass.coe_eq_one.mp h), fun d hd hd4 => ?_⟩
    obtain ⟨e, he⟩ := hd
    have he4 : e % 4 = 1 := by
      have h := hx4
      rw [he, Nat.mul_mod, hd4, one_mul, Nat.mod_mod] at h
      exact h
    rcases ha.2 ⟨d, hd4⟩ ⟨e, he4⟩ (Subtype.ext he) with h | h
    · exact Or.inl (congrArg Subtype.val h)
    · have he1 : e = 1 := congrArg Subtype.val h
      subst he1
      exact Or.inr (by rw [he, mul_one])
  · rintro ⟨h1, hdiv⟩
    refine ⟨fun h => h1 (by rw [h]; rfl), fun y z hyz => ?_⟩
    have hyz' : (x : ℕ) = y * z := congrArg Subtype.val hyz
    have hy4 : (y : ℕ) % 4 = 1 := y.2
    rcases hdiv y ⟨z, hyz'⟩ hy4 with h | h
    · exact Or.inl (OneMemClass.coe_eq_one.mp h)
    · right
      apply OneMemClass.coe_eq_one.mp
      have hx0 : (x : ℕ) ≠ 0 := by omega
      rw [h] at hyz'
      exact (Nat.mul_eq_left hx0).mp hyz'.symm

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] A bounded check of the divisors decides a first arrival of Hilbert's
monoid. -/
theorem hilbert_atom_of_check (n : ℕ) (hn : n % 4 = 1)
    (h : n ≠ 1 ∧ ∀ d < n + 1, d ∣ n → d % 4 = 1 → d = 1 ∨ d = n) : Atom (hil n hn) := by
  rw [hilbert_atom_iff]
  refine ⟨h.1, fun d hd hd4 => h.2 d ?_ hd hd4⟩
  have hn0 : 0 < n := by omega
  exact Nat.lt_succ_of_le (Nat.le_of_dvd hn0 hd)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **`9`, `21` and `49` are first arrivals of Hilbert's monoid.** -/
theorem hilbert_atoms : Atom (hil 9) ∧ Atom (hil 21) ∧ Atom (hil 49) :=
  ⟨hilbert_atom_of_check 9 _ (by decide), hilbert_atom_of_check 21 _ (by decide),
    hilbert_atom_of_check 49 _ (by decide)⟩

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] `9 · 49 = 21 · 21 = 441` in Hilbert's monoid. -/
theorem hilbert_mul : hil 9 * hil 49 = hil 21 * hil 21 ∧ hil 9 * hil 49 = hil 441 :=
  ⟨Subtype.ext rfl, Subtype.ext rfl⟩

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **Factorization into first arrivals is plural**: `{9, 49}` and `{21, 21}`
are two multisets of atoms with one product. -/
theorem hilbert_factorization_plural :
    ∃ s u : Multiset hilbert, (∀ a ∈ s, Atom a) ∧ (∀ a ∈ u, Atom a) ∧ s.prod = u.prod ∧ s ≠ u := by
  obtain ⟨h9, h21, h49⟩ := hilbert_atoms
  refine ⟨{hil 9, hil 49}, {hil 21, hil 21}, ?_, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro a ha
    simp only [Multiset.insert_eq_cons, Multiset.mem_cons, Multiset.mem_singleton] at ha
    rcases ha with rfl | rfl
    · exact h9
    · exact h49
  · intro a ha
    simp only [Multiset.insert_eq_cons, Multiset.mem_cons, Multiset.mem_singleton, or_self] at ha
    rw [ha]
    exact h21
  · simp only [Multiset.insert_eq_cons, Multiset.prod_cons, Multiset.prod_singleton]
    exact hilbert_mul.1
  · intro h
    have h9mem : hil 9 ∈ ({hil 9, hil 49} : Multiset hilbert) := by simp
    rw [h] at h9mem
    simp only [Multiset.insert_eq_cons, Multiset.mem_cons, Multiset.mem_singleton, or_self] at h9mem
    exact absurd (congrArg Subtype.val h9mem) (by decide)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **A first arrival need not be prime**: `21 ∣ 9 · 49`, `21 ∤ 9`, `21 ∤ 49`. -/
theorem hilbert_atom_not_prime : hil 21 ∣ hil 9 * hil 49 ∧ ¬ hil 21 ∣ hil 9 ∧ ¬ hil 21 ∣ hil 49 := by
  refine ⟨⟨hil 21, hilbert_mul.1⟩, fun h => ?_, fun h => ?_⟩
  · have hle := hilbert_isSize.le_of_dvd h
    change (21 : ℕ) ≤ 9 at hle
    omega
  · have hd := map_dvd hilbert.subtype h
    change (21 : ℕ) ∣ 49 at hd
    omega

end Hilbert

/-! ## 6. Monic polynomials over a finite field -/

section Monic

open Polynomial

variable (K : Type*) [Field K]

/-- [definition] The monic polynomials over `K`, a submonoid of `K[X]`. -/
def monics : Submonoid K[X] where
  carrier := {f | f.Monic}
  one_mem' := monic_one
  mul_mem' := fun ha hb => Monic.mul ha hb

variable {K}

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **The first arrivals of the monics are the monic irreducibles.** -/
theorem monic_atom_iff_irreducible (f : monics K) : Atom f ↔ Irreducible (f : K[X]) := by
  have hf : (f : K[X]).Monic := f.2
  constructor
  · intro ha
    have hf1 : (f : K[X]) ≠ 1 := fun h => ha.1 (OneMemClass.coe_eq_one.mp h)
    rw [irreducible_of_monic hf hf1]
    intro a b ha' hb' hab
    rcases ha.2 ⟨a, ha'⟩ ⟨b, hb'⟩ (Subtype.ext hab.symm) with h | h
    · exact Or.inl (congrArg Subtype.val h)
    · exact Or.inr (congrArg Subtype.val h)
  · intro hirr
    have hf1 : (f : K[X]) ≠ 1 := hirr.ne_one
    refine ⟨fun h => hf1 (by rw [h]; rfl), fun y z hyz => ?_⟩
    rcases (irreducible_of_monic hf hf1).mp hirr y z y.2 z.2 (congrArg Subtype.val hyz).symm with h | h
    · exact Or.inl (OneMemClass.coe_eq_one.mp h)
    · exact Or.inr (OneMemClass.coe_eq_one.mp h)

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Divisibility among monics is divisibility of polynomials. -/
theorem monics_coe_dvd {p q : monics K} (h : p ∣ q) : (p : K[X]) ∣ q := by
  obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := h
  exact ⟨c, Submonoid.coe_mul _ _ _⟩

variable (K) [Fintype K]

/-- [definition] **The size of a monic**: `|K| ^ deg f`, the count of residues modulo `f`. -/
noncomputable def polySize : monics K →* ℕ where
  toFun f := Fintype.card K ^ (f : K[X]).natDegree
  map_one' := by simp
  map_mul' f g := by
    simp only [Submonoid.coe_mul]
    rw [Monic.natDegree_mul f.2 g.2, pow_add]

variable {K}

/-- [definition] The size of a monic, unfolded. -/
theorem polySize_apply (f : monics K) : polySize K f = Fintype.card K ^ (f : K[X]).natDegree := rfl

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] `|K| ^ deg` is a size on the monics. -/
theorem polySize_isSize : IsSize (polySize K) := by
  intro f hf
  have hdeg : (f : K[X]).natDegree ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    exact hf (OneMemClass.coe_eq_one.mp ((Monic.natDegree_eq_zero f.2).mp h0))
  rw [polySize_apply]
  exact Nat.one_lt_pow hdeg Fintype.one_lt_card

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] Every monic is a product of monic irreducibles, read from item 1. -/
theorem monic_factors (f : K[X]) (hf : f.Monic) :
    ∃ s : Multiset K[X], (∀ g ∈ s, g.Monic ∧ Irreducible g) ∧ s.prod = f := by
  obtain ⟨s, hs, hprod⟩ := exists_atom_factors polySize_isSize (⟨f, hf⟩ : monics K)
  refine ⟨s.map Subtype.val, fun g hg => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩ := Multiset.mem_map.mp hg
    exact ⟨a.2, (monic_atom_iff_irreducible a).mp (hs a ha)⟩
  · rw [← Submonoid.coe_multiset_prod, hprod]

/-- [proved-standard; formal-checked] **Coverage for monics**: a monic `f ≠ 1` with no monic irreducible factor `g`
of `2 deg g ≤ deg f` is irreducible. -/
theorem irreducible_of_no_small_factor (f : K[X]) (hf : f.Monic) (hf1 : f ≠ 1)
    (h : ∀ g : K[X], g.Monic → Irreducible g → 2 * g.natDegree ≤ f.natDegree → ¬ g ∣ f) : Irreducible f := by
  have hx1 : (⟨f, hf⟩ : monics K) ≠ 1 := fun h1 => hf1 (congrArg Subtype.val h1)
  have hq : 1 < Fintype.card K := Fintype.one_lt_card
  have ha := atom_of_no_small_atom_dvd polySize_isSize hx1 fun p hp hsq hdvd => by
    rw [polySize_apply, polySize_apply, ← pow_add, ← two_mul] at hsq
    exact h p p.2 ((monic_atom_iff_irreducible p).mp hp) ((Nat.pow_le_pow_iff_right hq).mp hsq)
      (monics_coe_dvd hdvd)
  exact (monic_atom_iff_irreducible _).mp ha

end Monic

end Holonics.Compression.Landmark.SieveTower
